---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Sources from '../components/Sources.astro';
import RelatedTopics from '../components/RelatedTopics.astro';
import VerifiedDate from '../components/VerifiedDate.astro';
import { LAYERS, TASKS, TOGGLE_BLOCKS, SCENARIOS } from '../lib/architecture';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Architecture"
  description="Why the same task can touch one file or ten, how an AI pipeline is actually wired, and how to weigh real architectural tradeoffs — three labs, one workspace."
>
  <p class="eyebrow"><a href="/systems/">← Systems</a></p>
  <h1>Architecture</h1>
  <VerifiedDate />

  <div class="workspace-page">
    <div class="workspace-shell">
      <aside class="docs-panel">
        <section class="docs-block">
          <p class="docs-label">TL;DR</p>
          <ul>
            <li>Architecture is <strong>where a decision lives</strong>, not just how many layers you drew.</li>
            <li>Good boundaries keep a change contained; broken ones spread it everywhere, including into whatever's reading your code — human or agent.</li>
            <li>An "AI pipeline" is a normal request path with an LLM in it — the same rules about valid paths and dead ends still apply.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>
        <section class="docs-block">
          <p class="docs-label">ELI5</p>
          <ul>
            <li>A tidy house: fix the sink, you go to the kitchen. Nothing else moves.</li>
            <li>A messy house where the plumbing runs through every room: fix the sink, you're crawling through the whole house.</li>
            <li>Same sink. Different house. <strong>That difference is architecture.</strong></li>
          </ul>
        </section>
        <section class="docs-block">
          <p class="docs-label">Technical definition</p>
          <ul>
            <li>Architecture is the set of <strong>boundaries and dependency rules</strong> between a system's parts — who's allowed to call whom, and over what contract.</li>
            <li>A change's "blast radius" is every file that has to change because of it — not a metaphor, a countable thing.</li>
            <li>An AI pipeline is architecture like any other: fixed entry/exit (client, API) and a request path through whatever sits behind it.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>
        <section class="docs-block">
          <p class="docs-label">Why it matters</p>
          <ul>
            <li>An AI coding agent works from whatever files it can see — the smaller a task's real blast radius, the smaller the context it needs and the safer its edit is.</li>
            <li>A tangled boundary doesn't just slow humans down; it inflates exactly the context window an agent has to reason over.</li>
            <li>Wiring an LLM into a system is still a systems-design problem first — where the call lives changes latency, cost, and who can reuse it.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>
        <section class="docs-block">
          <p class="docs-label">When to use what</p>
          <ul>
            <li>Knowing the pieces isn't the skill — knowing <strong>which one a given task actually needs</strong> is. That judgment call is what the three labs below are for.</li>
            <li><strong>Plain endpoint, no LLM:</strong> the task is deterministic — the answer follows fixed rules. Don't reach for a model because you can.</li>
            <li><strong>+ Orchestrator + LLM:</strong> the task needs judgment or language generation, and the model already knows enough on its own.</li>
            <li><strong>+ Retrieval:</strong> the model needs facts it wasn't trained on — your docs, your database, anything that changes after training.</li>
            <li><strong>+ Tools:</strong> the model needs to <em>do</em> something, not just say something — call an API, run code, change a record.</li>
            <li><strong>Invest in clean layering</strong> exactly where more than one kind of change (or more than one kind of reader — human, or agent) will touch that code again.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>
        <section class="docs-block">
          <p class="docs-label">Failure modes</p>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>"More layers is always better."</strong> The Codebase lab's phone-number task shows a case where wide blast radius is correct, not a smell.</li>
            <li><strong>"Adding an LLM call makes it an AI pipeline."</strong> Try the AI Pipeline lab with no orchestrator — it's a valid, ordinary endpoint that happens to exist.</li>
            <li><strong>"There's one right architecture."</strong> The Compare lab's options are all viable — the right one depends on constraints the diagram alone won't show you.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>
      </aside>

      <div class="workspace-main">
        <div class="workspace-toolbar">
          <span class="workspace-title">architecture.lab</span>
          <span class="workspace-hint">three modes, one workspace — switch tabs below</span>
        </div>

        <div class="tabs" role="tablist" aria-label="Architecture labs">
          <button type="button" class="tab-btn active" role="tab" aria-selected="true" aria-controls="panel-codebase" id="tab-codebase" data-tab="codebase">Codebase</button>
          <button type="button" class="tab-btn" role="tab" aria-selected="false" aria-controls="panel-pipeline" id="tab-pipeline" data-tab="pipeline">AI Pipeline</button>
          <button type="button" class="tab-btn" role="tab" aria-selected="false" aria-controls="panel-compare" id="tab-compare" data-tab="compare">Compare</button>
        </div>

        <!-- ===== Codebase tab ===== -->
        <div class="tab-panel active" id="panel-codebase" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="tab-codebase">
          <p class="lab-note">
            Pick a task, then flip the boundary quality. Same task, same
            starting point — watch which layers light up.
          </p>

          <div class="control-row">
            <label class="control-label" for="task-select">Task</label>
            <select id="task-select" class="select-input">
              {TASKS.map((t) => <option value={t.id}>{t.title}</option>)}
            </select>
          </div>

          <div class="control-row">
            <span class="control-label">Boundary quality</span>
            <div class="segmented" role="radiogroup" aria-label="Boundary quality">
              <button type="button" class="seg-btn active" data-quality="clean" role="radio" aria-checked="true">Clean layering</button>
              <button type="button" class="seg-btn" data-quality="tangled" role="radio" aria-checked="false">Tangled boundaries</button>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="layer-stack" role="img" aria-label="UI, API, service, and data layers">
            {LAYERS.map((l) => (
              <div class="layer-node" data-layer={l.id}>
                <span class="layer-name">{l.name}</span>
              </div>
            ))}
          </div>

          <p class="blast-note" id="blast-note"></p>
        </div>

        <!-- ===== AI Pipeline tab ===== -->
        <div class="tab-panel" id="panel-pipeline" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="tab-pipeline" hidden>
          <p class="lab-note">
            Client and API are fixed. Toggle what sits behind the gateway,
            then run a request — an invalid combination fails with a real reason, not a canned error.
          </p>

          <div class="toggle-row">
            {TOGGLE_BLOCKS.map((b) => (
              <div class="toggle-item">
                <button type="button" class="toggle-chip" data-block={b.id} aria-pressed="false">{b.name}</button>
                <p class="toggle-hint">{b.whenToUse}</p>
              </div>
            ))}
          </div>

          <div class="pipeline" role="img" aria-label="Client, API gateway, and toggleable blocks behind it">
            <div class="pipe-node fixed active" data-pnode="client"><span class="pipe-icon" aria-hidden="true">▣</span><span class="pipe-name">Client</span></div>
            <div class="pipe-edge"></div>
            <div class="pipe-node fixed" data-pnode="api"><span class="pipe-icon" aria-hidden="true">▤</span><span class="pipe-name">API</span></div>
            <div class="pipe-edge"></div>
            <div class="pipe-node dim" data-pnode="orchestrator"><span class="pipe-icon" aria-hidden="true">◆</span><span class="pipe-name">Orchestrator</span></div>
            <div class="pipe-edge"></div>
            <div class="pipe-node dim" data-pnode="llm"><span class="pipe-icon" aria-hidden="true">✦</span><span class="pipe-name">LLM</span></div>
          </div>
          <div class="pipeline-extra">
            <div class="pipe-node dim small" data-pnode="retrieval"><span class="pipe-name">Retrieval</span></div>
            <div class="pipe-node dim small" data-pnode="tools"><span class="pipe-name">Tools</span></div>
          </div>

          <div class="generate-row">
            <button type="button" id="run-pipeline-btn" class="ex-btn">Run request →</button>
          </div>
          <div class="trace-log" id="pipeline-log" aria-live="polite"></div>
        </div>

        <!-- ===== Compare tab ===== -->
        <div class="tab-panel" id="panel-compare" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="tab-compare" hidden>
          <p class="lab-note">Pick a real scenario, then weigh the options side by side.</p>

          <div class="control-row">
            <label class="control-label" for="scenario-select">Scenario</label>
            <select id="scenario-select" class="select-input">
              {SCENARIOS.map((s) => <option value={s.id}>{s.title}</option>)}
            </select>
          </div>
          <p class="scenario-prompt" id="scenario-prompt"></p>

          <div class="options-grid" id="options-grid"></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="footer-page">
    <RelatedTopics />

    <Sources
      sources={[
        {
          title: 'Multitier architecture — Wikipedia',
          url: 'https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Multitier_architecture',
          note: 'The layered split this lab\'s Codebase tab is built on.',
        },
        {
          title: 'Hexagonal architecture (ports and adapters) — Alistair Cockburn',
          url: 'https://alistair.cockburn.us/hexagonal-architecture/',
          note: 'The general principle behind keeping business logic isolated from any one boundary — why a "tangled" version of a task spreads further.',
        },
        {
          title: 'Retrieval-augmented generation (RAG) — original paper',
          url: 'https://arxiv.org/abs/2005.11401',
          note: 'What the AI Pipeline tab\'s "retrieval" block is actually modeling.',
        },
        {
          title: 'Model Context Protocol',
          url: 'https://modelcontextprotocol.io',
          note: 'The real standard for how an orchestrator hands tool access to an LLM, modeled by this lab\'s "tools" block.',
        },
      ]}
    />
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<script>
  import { scrambleText as decode } from '../lib/decode';
  import {
    getBlastRadius, runPipeline, getScenario, LAYERS,
    type LayerId, type BoundaryQuality, type ToggleBlockId, type PipelineBlock,
  } from '../lib/architecture';

  // ---- Codebase tab ----
  const taskSelect = document.getElementById('task-select') as HTMLSelectElement;
  const qualityBtns = document.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>('.seg-btn');
  const layerNodes: Record<LayerId, HTMLElement> = {} as Record<LayerId, HTMLElement>;
  for (const l of LAYERS) layerNodes[l.id] = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>(`[data-layer="${l.id}"]`)!;
  const blastNote = document.getElementById('blast-note')!;
  let quality: BoundaryQuality = 'clean';

  function renderBlastRadius() {
    for (const el of Object.values(layerNodes)) el.classList.remove('active');
    const { layers, note } = getBlastRadius(taskSelect.value, quality);
    for (const id of layers) layerNodes[id].classList.add('active');
    decode(blastNote, `${layers.length} of ${LAYERS.length} layers touched — ${note}`, { frames: 5, frameMs: 20 });
  }

  taskSelect.addEventListener('change', renderBlastRadius);
  qualityBtns.forEach((btn) => btn.addEventListener('click', () => {
    quality = btn.dataset.quality as BoundaryQuality;
    qualityBtns.forEach((b) => { b.classList.toggle('active', b === btn); b.setAttribute('aria-checked', String(b === btn)); });
    renderBlastRadius();
  }));
  renderBlastRadius();

  // ---- AI Pipeline tab ----
  const toggleChips = document.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>('.toggle-chip');
  const enabled = new Set<ToggleBlockId>();
  const pipeNodes: Record<PipelineBlock, HTMLElement> = {
    client: document.querySelector('[data-pnode="client"]')!,
    api: document.querySelector('[data-pnode="api"]')!,
    orchestrator: document.querySelector('[data-pnode="orchestrator"]')!,
    llm: document.querySelector('[data-pnode="llm"]')!,
    retrieval: document.querySelector('[data-pnode="retrieval"]')!,
    tools: document.querySelector('[data-pnode="tools"]')!,
  };
  const pipelineLog = document.getElementById('pipeline-log')!;
  const runPipelineBtn = document.getElementById('run-pipeline-btn') as HTMLButtonElement;
  let pipelineTimer: number | undefined;
  // Bumped on every run so a still-animating decode() from a superseded
  // run (its own internal timer, not `pipelineTimer`) can tell it's
  // stale and stop instead of appending a stray row into the next run's
  // already-cleared log.
  let pipelineRunId = 0;

  toggleChips.forEach((chip) => chip.addEventListener('click', () => {
    const id = chip.dataset.block as ToggleBlockId;
    const on = !enabled.has(id);
    if (on) enabled.add(id); else enabled.delete(id);
    chip.setAttribute('aria-pressed', String(on));
    chip.classList.toggle('active', on);
    pipeNodes[id].classList.toggle('dim', !on);
    pipeNodes[id].classList.toggle('active', on);
  }));

  function runPipelineLab() {
    if (pipelineTimer) { clearTimeout(pipelineTimer); pipelineTimer = undefined; }
    const runId = ++pipelineRunId;
    pipelineLog.innerHTML = '';
    for (const [id, el] of Object.entries(pipeNodes)) {
      if (id === 'client' || id === 'api') continue;
      el.classList.remove('running');
    }
    const result = runPipeline(enabled);

    if (!result.valid) {
      const row = document.createElement('div');
      row.className = 'trace-row trace-error';
      row.textContent = `✕ ${result.error}`;
      pipelineLog.append(row);
      return;
    }

    let i = 0;
    const step = () => {
      if (runId !== pipelineRunId) return;
      for (const el of Object.values(pipeNodes)) el.classList.remove('running');
      if (i >= result.log.length) return;
      const entry = result.log[i];
      pipeNodes[entry.block].classList.add('running');
      const row = document.createElement('div');
      row.className = 'trace-row';
      const label = document.createElement('span');
      label.className = 'trace-label';
      label.textContent = entry.block.toUpperCase();
      const text = document.createElement('span');
      text.className = 'trace-text';
      row.append(label, text);
      pipelineLog.append(row);
      pipelineLog.scrollTop = pipelineLog.scrollHeight;
      decode(text, entry.text, { frames: 5, frameMs: 20, onDone: () => {
        if (runId !== pipelineRunId) return;
        i++;
        pipelineTimer = window.setTimeout(step, 260);
      }});
    };
    step();
  }
  runPipelineBtn.addEventListener('click', runPipelineLab);

  // ---- Compare tab ----
  const scenarioSelect = document.getElementById('scenario-select') as HTMLSelectElement;
  const scenarioPrompt = document.getElementById('scenario-prompt')!;
  const optionsGrid = document.getElementById('options-grid')!;

  function renderScenario() {
    const scenario = getScenario(scenarioSelect.value);
    scenarioPrompt.textContent = scenario.prompt;
    optionsGrid.innerHTML = '';
    for (const opt of scenario.options) {
      const card = document.createElement('div');
      card.className = 'option-card';
      const title = document.createElement('p');
      title.className = 'option-title';
      title.textContent = opt.title;
      const summary = document.createElement('p');
      summary.className = 'option-summary';
      summary.textContent = opt.summary;
      const pros = document.createElement('ul');
      pros.className = 'option-list pros';
      for (const p of opt.pros) { const li = document.createElement('li'); li.textContent = p; pros.append(li); }
      const cons = document.createElement('ul');
      cons.className = 'option-list cons';
      for (const c of opt.cons) { const li = document.createElement('li'); li.textContent = c; cons.append(li); }
      card.append(title, summary, pros, cons);
      optionsGrid.append(card);
    }
  }
  scenarioSelect.addEventListener('change', renderScenario);
  renderScenario();

  // ---- Tabs ----
  const tabBtns = document.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>('.tab-btn');
  const tabPanels = document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('.tab-panel');
  tabBtns.forEach((btn) => btn.addEventListener('click', () => {
    tabBtns.forEach((b) => { b.classList.toggle('active', b === btn); b.setAttribute('aria-selected', String(b === btn)); });
    tabPanels.forEach((p) => {
      const show = p.id === `panel-${btn.dataset.tab}`;
      p.classList.toggle('active', show);
      p.hidden = !show;
    });
  }));
</script>

<style>
  .workspace-page {
    position: relative; left: 50%; transform: translateX(-50%);
    width: 100vw; max-width: 92rem; box-sizing: border-box;
    padding: 0 var(--sp-5);
    margin: var(--sp-5) 0 var(--sp-6);
  }
  .workspace-shell {
    border: 1px solid var(--line); background: var(--bg-1);
    display: grid; grid-template-columns: 34rem 1fr;
  }
  @media (max-width: 60rem) {
    .workspace-shell { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .docs-panel { order: 2; position: static; border-right: none; border-top: 1px solid var(--line); }
    .workspace-main { order: 1; }
  }

  .docs-panel {
    display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(15rem, 1fr));
    gap: var(--sp-3); align-content: start; position: sticky; top: var(--sp-4);
    padding: var(--sp-4); border-right: 1px solid var(--line);
  }
  .docs-block { border: 1px solid var(--line); background: var(--bg-0); padding: var(--sp-3); }
  .docs-label { font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 0.64rem; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.08em; color: var(--accent); margin: 0 0 var(--sp-2); }
  .docs-block ul { margin: 0; padding-left: 1.1rem; display: grid; gap: var(--sp-2); font-size: 0.76rem; line-height: 1.4; color: var(--text-1); }

  .workspace-main { min-width: 0; container-type: inline-size; display: grid; gap: var(--sp-4); align-content: start; padding: var(--sp-4); }
  .workspace-toolbar { display: flex; align-items: baseline; gap: var(--sp-3); flex-wrap: wrap; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); padding-bottom: var(--sp-3); }
  .workspace-title { font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: var(--step--1); font-weight: 700; color: var(--accent); letter-spacing: 0.02em; }
  .workspace-hint { font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 0.68rem; color: var(--text-2); }

  .footer-page {
    position: relative; left: 50%; transform: translateX(-50%);
    width: 100vw; max-width: 92rem; box-sizing: border-box;
    padding: 0 var(--sp-5);
  }
  .footer-page :global(.sources-list),
  .footer-page :global(.related-list) {
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(18rem, 1fr));
  }

  .tabs { display: flex; gap: var(--sp-2); flex-wrap: wrap; }
  .tab-btn {
    font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 0.74rem; padding: var(--sp-2) var(--sp-3);
    background: var(--bg-0); border: 1px solid var(--line-bright); color: var(--text-1); cursor: pointer;
  }
  .tab-btn:hover { color: var(--text-0); }
  .tab-btn.active { border-color: var(--accent); color: var(--accent); background: var(--bg-2); }

  .tab-panel { display: none; }
  .tab-panel.active { display: grid; gap: var(--sp-4); }

  .lab-note { color: var(--text-2); font-size: var(--step--1); margin: 0; }

  .control-row { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: var(--sp-3); flex-wrap: wrap; }
  .control-label { font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 0.7rem; color: var(--text-2); text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.06em; }
  .select-input {
    font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 0.78rem; padding: var(--sp-2); flex: 1; min-width: 14rem;
    background: var(--bg-0); border: 1px solid var(--line-bright); color: var(--text-0);
  }
  .segmented { display: flex; gap: 0; border: 1px solid var(--line-bright); }
  .seg-btn { font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 0.7rem; padding: var(--sp-2) var(--sp-3); background: var(--bg-0); border: none; color: var(--text-1); cursor: pointer; }
  .seg-btn + .seg-btn { border-left: 1px solid var(--line-bright); }
  .seg-btn.active { background: var(--accent); color: var(--bg-0); font-weight: 700; }

  /* codebase layer stack */
  .layer-stack { display: grid; gap: var(--sp-2); }
  .layer-node {
    padding: var(--sp-3); border: 1px solid var(--line-bright); background: var(--bg-0);
    font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: var(--step--1); color: var(--text-1); transition: all 150ms ease-out;
  }
  .layer-node.active { border-color: var(--status-broken); color: var(--text-0); box-shadow: 0 0 0 1px var(--status-broken), 0 0 16px color-mix(in srgb, var(--status-broken) 35%, transparent); }
  .blast-note { font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 0.72rem; color: var(--text-1); padding: var(--sp-3); background: var(--bg-0); border: 1px solid var(--line); min-height: 2.5rem; }

  /* pipeline (shared visual language with the pipeline lab) */
  .toggle-row { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(13rem, 1fr)); gap: var(--sp-3); }
  .toggle-item { display: grid; gap: var(--sp-1); align-content: start; }
  .toggle-chip { font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 0.72rem; padding: var(--sp-2) var(--sp-3); background: var(--bg-0); border: 1px solid var(--line); color: var(--text-1); cursor: pointer; }
  .toggle-chip:hover { border-color: var(--accent); }
  .toggle-chip.active { border-color: var(--accent); color: var(--accent); background: var(--bg-2); }
  .toggle-hint { font-size: 0.68rem; color: var(--text-2); margin: 0; line-height: 1.35; }

  .pipeline { display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; gap: 0; flex-wrap: wrap; }
  .pipe-node {
    display: flex; flex-direction: column; align-items: center; gap: var(--sp-1);
    padding: var(--sp-3); border: 1px solid var(--line-bright); background: var(--bg-0);
    min-width: 8rem; text-align: center; transition: all 150ms ease-out;
  }
  .pipe-node.dim { opacity: 0.4; }
  .pipe-node.active { opacity: 1; border-color: var(--accent); }
  .pipe-node.running { border-color: var(--accent); box-shadow: 0 0 0 1px var(--accent), 0 0 18px color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 40%, transparent); }
  .pipe-icon { font-size: var(--step-2); color: var(--text-1); }
  .pipe-node.active .pipe-icon, .pipe-node.running .pipe-icon { color: var(--accent); }
  .pipe-name { font-family: var(--font-mono); font-weight: 700; color: var(--text-0); font-size: var(--step--1); letter-spacing: 0.04em; }
  .pipe-edge { flex: 0 0 auto; width: 2.5rem; height: 2px; background: var(--line-bright); }
  .pipeline-extra { display: flex; justify-content: center; gap: var(--sp-3); }
  .pipe-node.small { min-width: 6rem; padding: var(--sp-2); }

  .generate-row { margin: 0; }
  .ex-btn {
    font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: var(--step--1); padding: var(--sp-2) var(--sp-3);
    background: var(--bg-0); border: 1px solid var(--line-bright); color: var(--text-1); cursor: pointer;
  }
  .ex-btn:hover { border-color: var(--accent); color: var(--text-0); }

  .trace-log {
    min-height: 6rem; max-height: 16rem; overflow-y: auto; padding: var(--sp-3);
    background: var(--bg-0); border: 1px solid var(--line-bright);
    font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: var(--step--1); display: grid; gap: var(--sp-2);
  }
  /* :global() because these rows are assembled with createElement in the
     <script> below -- Astro's scoped-style hash only lands on elements
     written directly in this file's template, so a plain scoped
     selector here would silently never match. */
  :global(.trace-row) { display: flex; gap: var(--sp-3); }
  :global(.trace-label) { flex-shrink: 0; width: 6rem; letter-spacing: 0.06em; font-weight: 700; color: var(--accent); }
  :global(.trace-text) { color: var(--text-1); }
  :global(.trace-error) { color: var(--status-broken); }

  /* compare */
  .scenario-prompt { color: var(--text-1); font-size: var(--step--1); margin: 0; }
  .options-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(14rem, 1fr)); gap: var(--sp-3); }
